    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0573" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.61A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>)<anchor n="7" xml:id="d668-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-03T10:00:00+02:00">February 3,
                            1942—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>190. My 2049, December 30, 11 a.m., and my 189, February 3, 9 a.m.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d668-f2"/> Has the Department any information as to the appointment
                    of an agricultural expert to Saudi Arabia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d668-f1" n="7" type="source" xml:id="d668-f1-content">
                <p>Also accredited as Minister to Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d668-f2" n="8" xml:id="d668-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
